 features a social learning component that allows students to connect with peers, ask questions, and collaborate on projects. The platform is accessible on both web and mobile devices, making it convenient for students to learn on-the-go. Our team is considering adding several new features to LearnSphere, including an AI-powered adaptive learning engine that can adjust the difficulty level and content of courses based on a student's performance, a virtual reality (VR) and augmented reality (AR) component that can enhance the learning experience through immersive simulations, and a gamification feature that rewards students for achieving milestones and completing challenging tasks. We also plan to integrate LearnSphere with popular productivity and organization tools, such as Google Calendar and Trello, to help students better manage their time and stay organized. Additionally, we aim to expand the platform's content offerings to include more courses and resources on emerging technologies, such as artificial intelligence, blockchain, and cybersecurity.","strict":"true","timeout":"0"},"stack":[{"file":"/Users/karthiku/playwright-js-project/pages/hercules/HerculesSurveyGenerator.js","line":174,"column":36,"function":"HerculesSurveyGenerator.handleTextInputFallback"}]}
